   669	### 11. Enforcement while the reservation stands
   670	
   671	`tools/validate.py` carries a deterministic boundary gate that runs on every
   672	validation. It:
   673	
   674	1. requires this decision to fix both closed sets by name, both artifact
   675	   classes, the boundary failure classes, both execution-policy identities, the
   676	   reserved evidence-record version, and the toolchain requirement object;
   677	2. forbids this decision from naming a deferred hardened guarantee;
   678	3. rejects any occurrence of a reserved driver identifier or the reserved policy
   679	   identity on a surface file outside `decisions/`, because a decision record is
   680	   where an identifier is proposed, reserved, and retired while every other
   681	   surface is admission;
   682	4. proves the reserved capability-evidence record version un-admitted
   683	   positively rather than by absence, by requiring the frozen corpus to keep
   684	   rejecting it — absence would be the wrong test, because that version already
   685	   appears in the rc.5 corpus and release gate as the example of a version that
   686	   MUST be rejected;
   687	5. requires every driver-bearing schema definition to close `driver` with a
   688	   `const` over the admitted wire driver set and to require it;
   689	6. checks every driver-bearing definition against a **closed exact member-set
   690	   table** rather than a deny-list — each definition's property set, required
   691	   set, and `additionalProperties: false` must match the table exactly, and a
   692	   driver-bearing definition missing from the table is itself a failure, so no
