      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check
      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)
      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)

codex
The second issue is also confirmed in the decision itself: it allows a rejected driver contract to retire an identifier unused and tells integration to admit only accepted contracts, but later requires claim schema 4 to admit all eight identifiers. That makes the permitted Kotlin-retirement path impossible to implement without violating one of the decision’s own rules.

I’m recording both as ordinary implementation rework (`to-dev`), not a stop-the-line blocker.
